# escape_puca_snare -- the deeps: a púca caught in the ghouls' snare, in the side cave off the second chamber
#
# PLACEHOLDERS: each card says what happens. The real words (and their Irish) to be written.
# A trickster who has tricked itself into a bind. Its last card sets escape_puca_snare_free: it goes.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 1

= node 0 — caught
@when !note escape_puca_snare_free
@continue
[PLACEHOLDER] The púca, lashed in the ghouls' snare, sees you.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
It tells you how it came to be caught (its own trick, gone wrong), and begs you to cut it loose.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= node 1 — loosed
@when !note escape_puca_snare_free
@note escape_puca_snare_free
[PLACEHOLDER] You cut the cords. It thanks you in its fashion, and is gone.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
